00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:14.340
Hello, and welcome to another edition of modeling the masters. My name is Evan Carmichael and today

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:20.760
We're going to be talking about the famous entrepreneur walt Disney and how you can model his strategies to achieve success with your business

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:56.279
Everyone knows walt Disney for his movies theme parks and cast of characters. What most people don't know is when he first started out?

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.780
He had no money he had to live in his office because he couldn't afford [write] for an apartment

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:04.769
And he survived on a diet of cold beans because he couldn't afford food

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.739
By committing to his business and sticking with it

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.790
He was now able to build a business [that] has almost 40 billion [dollars] in revenue

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:17.339
So [today], we're going to look at three lessons that you can learn for wealth is in success and apply it into your company

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:22.019
Lesson number one is find something that you love Walt Disney grew up in the early

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:25.890
1900's on a farm in Missouri and developed the passion for drawing

00:01:26.229 --> 00:01:32.609
So much, so that one of his neighbors actually paid him to draw some cartoons of his horses when Walt Disney got to school

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.050
He found that he was a good student

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:41.309
But he really enjoyed doodling as opposed to paying attention to his teachers he connected with one of his high school papers and started drawing

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.560
patriotic cartoons for the school paper

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:46.889
When he was 16, though he found that school just wasn't for him

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:49.200
So he dropped out join the red cross

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:54.720
Learn to become an ambulance driver, and actually was shipped to France to become an ambulance driver over there

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:58.199
He couldn't lose that passion for drawing and cartooning

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.099
And he ended up plastering his ambulance full of different cartoon creations that he had made

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:07.679
People knew him on the street because he was the ambulance driver with all the different cartoons blasted on his ambulance

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.229
He decided that cartooning was for him

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:14.848
he was going to be an artist and [return] to America to start his career as an artist, so

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:21.359
Lesson number one really is make sure you have that strong passion for your business if you don't really love it

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.529
It's going to be hard to succeed as a business owner if you look at any famous entrepreneur

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:31.500
And why they serve the business it wasn't for the money money comes when you're really passionate about what you're doing

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.640
So think about what is it that you do in your spare time? What do you really enjoy [doing]?

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:41.610
What gets you going in the morning? What are your hobbies, and how can you turn those into a potential business opportunity?

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:50.250
Lesson number two is push the boundaries Walt Disney first made his mark in 1934 when he proposed making a feature-length

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.810
Animation which had never been done [before] it was called snow white

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:59.789
Took three [years] to make [he] [went] a hundred percent over budget people thought he was crazy

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:05.670
For doing it you ran out of money at the end and had to actually act out the last scenes of the movie for his

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:10.890
Bankers to get the money he needed to close and finish the movie it ended up being a huge success

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:16.470
[it] was the biggest hit of the year [he] won an academy award for it, and it was a financial gain for him

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.789
Walt Disney's next big project was Disneyland [a]

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:28.860
338 Year project out in California a theme park which had nothing to do with his movies people thought he was crazy again

00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:31.979
Why would you do this what tie does it have to your movie business?

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:35.789
But he had a vision he [was] determined to make it happen and again

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:40.620
It was a big success for him then he went on to open up the Walt Disney world in, Florida

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:44.610
And the company was able to open up different theme parks around the world

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:52.230
So the message for entrepreneurs here is push the boundaries you need to do something different to get your company noticed as a small entrepreneur

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:57.390
[there's] so much competition. It's so difficult to get on people's radar screens and make them pay attention to you

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:00.119
So [you] have [to] do something that's going to get your notice

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.640
Something that will help you stand out from the crowd

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:08.189
So what is it that will be your equivalent of a snow white something that's never been done before [it's] really going to get you

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.469
Notice and get the attention paid [to] your business

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:13.529
Lesson number three is stay top of mind

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:19.019
Walt Disney did everything he could to make sure people kept remembering the Walt Disney name

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:25.169
He did a lot of advertising as an example. So we did TV campaigns direct mail campaigns print ads

00:04:25.169 --> 00:04:30.659
He even did grocery store coupon cutout so when you're at the grocery store, you're thinking about Walt Disney

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:37.710
He was also a pioneer in merchandising, so whenever a new feature film came out. That was a Walt Disney production

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:40.739
You would also be able to buy all the merchandise that went along with it

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.919
Today while Disney is [known] not only for its movies

00:04:43.919 --> 00:04:49.739
But its TV stations theme parks dolls toys games and a whole host of other merchandise

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.560
So the lesson for entrepreneurs is stay top of mind

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:56.310
You need to do whatever you can to make sure your customers are always

00:04:56.410 --> 00:05:03.209
Thinking about you the easiest way [to] grow a business is to [sell] more to your existing customers the hardest way to grow a business

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.340
is to go and try to find new

00:05:06.009 --> 00:05:09.759
So do whatever you can to make sure your customers are always thinking about you

00:05:09.759 --> 00:05:13.298
You're the first person that comes to mind when you're thinking about your product or service

00:05:13.299 --> 00:05:17.769
And it's the best way to be able to grow your business Walt Disney is an entrepreneurial legend

00:05:17.769 --> 00:05:24.039
Who's built up one of the most recognized companies in the world but remember when he first got started he had no money?

00:05:24.649 --> 00:05:29.379
Nobody believed in him he had to live out of his office because he couldn't afford an apartment

00:05:29.379 --> 00:05:36.759
And he survived on a diet of cold beans because he couldn't afford other food by following his lessons though you too can achieve

00:05:37.369 --> 00:05:41.319
entrepreneurial success so remember find something you love

00:05:41.899 --> 00:05:44.858
Push the boundaries and stay top of mind

